      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The aim of this study was to examine the duration of action of a single cutaneous application of a 10% isosorbide dinitrate ointment (ISDN-S) and also to ascertain the possible appearance of nitrate tolerance after 6--8 months' maintenance therapy with ISDN-S. After a single application of the ointment an effect lasting more than 7 hours was confirmed by bicycle ergometry. After longterm therapy an acute test with rapidly acting sublingual ISDN produced an undiminished response thus showing lack of nitrate tolerance."},
